'''Luke's hut''' was a [[Color|gray]] [[stone]] hut, made of several pieces of rock, located in the [[Jedi village]] on [[Temple Island]] on the [[planet]] [[Ahch-To]]. The hut served as the home of [[Jedi Master]] [[Luke Skywalker]] after he went into [[Exile (punishment)|exile]] following the [[Destruction of the Jedi Temple|destruction]] of his [[Jedi Temple of Luke Skywalker|Jedi temple]] at the hands of his nephew [[Ben Solo|Kylo Ren]]. Skywalker lived there<ref name="TLJ VD" /> until [[34 ABY]],<ref name="Date Note">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' places the events of [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']] in [[34 ABY]]. [[Star Wars: Episode VIII The Last Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VIII ''The Last Jedi'']] takes place immediately after the end of ''The Force Awakens''.</ref> when the [[Force-sensitive]] [[scavenger]] [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]] convinced him to [[Jedi training|train]] her to aid the [[Resistance]] in their [[First Order-Resistance War|war]] against the [[First Order]].<ref name="Episode VIII">{{Film|VIII}}</ref>

{{Struct-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
During the early development of the [[2017]] film [[Star Wars: Episode VIII The Last Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VIII ''The Last Jedi'']], [[Luke Skywalker]] was originally meant to be visited while meditating in his hut by the [[Force spirit]] of an all-powerful [[Sith Lord]] described to have ruled over the [[Dark side of the Force]] from the [[Netherworld of the Force]], pulling from behind the scenes "[[Supreme Leader]] [[Snoke]]'s strings."<ref name="Art TLJ">''[[The Art of Star Wars: The Last Jedi]]''</ref>

